WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:19.120
OK, so in the last 24 hours, the health questions
about Donald Trump have appeared not just

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.090
on Fox News, as we already talked about, but
the health questions around Trump have also

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.820
become a focus of a new ad from the Republican
pack.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.650
Republican political action committee called
the Lincoln Project.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.629
Now, we've talked about the Lincoln Project
a little bit before.

00:00:34.629 --> 00:00:36.780
It's a PAC run by some prominent Republicans.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.379
This includes George Conway, who, by the way,
is the husband of Trump adviser Kellyanne

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:41.420
Conway.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.539
Steve Schmidt is part of the Lincoln Project,
former McCain campaign manager Rick Wilson

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.729
and other prominent Republicans.

00:00:48.729 --> 00:00:56.110
They are a Republican PAC that realizes Trump
is a danger and must be removed.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.860
Their ads have been going after Trump harder
and harder.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:05.420
And yesterday they released an ad that goes
after Donald Trump on the topic of his health,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:11.979
again, raising questions about Trump's behavior
over the weekend at West Point, linking Trump's

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:17.280
behavior to the last minute visit to Walter
Reed Medical Center in 2019.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.689
So let's look at the ad.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:19.920
Let's listen to the ad.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.869
Now, some of these elements are visual, like,
for example, you'll hear voiceover and they

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:29.259
are showing Donald Trump acting bizarrely.

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.250
So I do recommend watching this online, but
you'll get a sense of the story that's being

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.140
told from the narration.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.140
Let's take a look.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.090
Something's wrong with Donald Trump.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.180
He's shaky.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:45.280
Weak chuckle Speaking of walking, so why are
we talking about this?

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.790
And why isn't the press covering Trump secretive
midnight run to Walter Reed Medical Center?

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:56.689
Why do so many reporters cover the White House
and pretend they can't see Trump's decline?

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:04.319
The most powerful office in the world needs
more than a week on shaky precedent.

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:09.370
Trump doesn't have the strength to lead North
a character to admit it.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.370
We're not doctors, but we're not blind.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:15.250
It's time we talk about this.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:18.570
Trump is not.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.170
Well.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.660
So this is really quite well done.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.850
Even the details down that down to the details,
it's very good.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:31.890
At one point when the voice over says we're
not doctors, what you see in the ad is Trump's

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.300
old doctor, Harold Bornstein, onscreen.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.240
That's the guy that Donald Trump allegedly
coerced into writing that bogus letter about

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.390
how healthy Donald Trump is.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.140
So we're now seeing this.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.260
I guess we would call it a sort of hashtag
movement.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.230
Trump is not well, is the name of it.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.810
And it's going much more mainstream than it
ever has.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.500
It's happening thanks to right wing media.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.050
It's happening thanks to a Republican political
action committee.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:05.370
And to go back to the analysis, this is not
about Republicans are now going to be widely

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.310
concerned about Donald Trump's health.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.510
That's not going to happen.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:13.830
The importance of this is that there are large
swaths of the American population that don't

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:18.490
even know that there has been a conversation
about Trump's health happening for three years.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:24.550
There's large portions of the electorate that
have no idea that dozens of medical experts,

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:30.190
both from the neuro neurology field and mental
health fields, have been expressing concern

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:34.510
about Donald Trump's health for years because
they watch Fox News and they only follow Republicans

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.620
on social media.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.570
They don't know about Trump's verbal glitches,
his wandering off.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.150
That time when he came off of Air Force One,
his limo was right in front of him.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:48.140
He wandered off, had to be brought back by
Secret Service, losing his train of thought,

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.840
sweating with the dilated pupils while speaking
upper Trump versus Downer Trump.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.040
They don't know about it.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:04:00.180
So even hearing about this as a thing on Fox
News and through a Republican pack is introducing

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.820
it into their awareness now.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.840
Ninety nine percent of them won't care.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.990
But remember that in 2016, the election came
down to seventy five thousand votes in three

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:10.990
states.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:16.730
We will mostly win if we get the turnout,
but we'll take any help we can get.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:22.220
And if it's a Republican pack and Fox News
asking even some questions about Donald Trump's

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.690
health, you might convince a few people and
we will take it.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.980
Now, there are reports about this ad being
controversial.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:36.540
For example, this there's an article this
morning in the week which is called New Lincoln

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.600
Project.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.590
Ad controversially questions Trump's health.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.200
It's not really controversial if you've been
following this for years.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.990
And there's a debate happening in this article
and elsewhere asking whether Trump's health

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.140
is fair game.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:56.500
Now, one argument is, listen, Trump mocked
a disabled reporter.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.980
He calls Joe Biden Sleepy Joe and says Joe
Biden doesn't even know what he's saying.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:05.940
He is regularly implying Joe Biden is cognitively
impaired.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.400
So that makes Trump's health fair game.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.540
I disagree with that assessment.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.880
The reason Trump's health is fair game is
because he's the president.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.800
And we have reason to believe that he's lying
about his health.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.040
His medical report lied about his height and
weight combination.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.800
He allegedly coerced the doctor to write a
letter saying Trump would be the healthiest

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.580
president in history.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:31.950
It's an empirical claim that no doctor could
actually make.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:36.680
So I understand the concern from disability
rights groups worried that this is bordering

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.380
on making fun of health issues.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.070
That is not what this is about.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.500
This is about understanding the critical nature
of being president.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.510
And when you have a president that no one
seems unwell.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:53.840
And number two is dishonest about everything,
including his height and weight.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.870
We are absolutely right to be concerned.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:07:17.070
That's really what this is fundamentally about.

